      "doc_type": "factbook",
      "title": "Official Statistics - Loyola Marymount University",
      "url": "https://academics.lmu.edu/officeofinstitutionalresearch/officialstatisticsandotherreporting/officialstatistics/",
      "summary": "The official statistics and other reporting section on the Loyola Marymount University website provides a comprehensive overview of current and historical trends on student enrollment and various student achievement metrics. Reports are developed by the Office of Institutional Research and Decision Support and include data on admissions, enrollment trends, retention and graduation rates, profiles of students and faculty, and degree completions. The site also offers insights into undergraduate major-switching patterns, retention rates for first-time and transfer students, and faculty and staff counts. The Common Data Set for LMU from 2008 to present can also be accessed.",
      "stored": false,
      "fetched_at": "2026-05-25T23:13:03.749846+05:30"
    },
    {
      "doc_type": "strategic_plan",
      "year": 2021,
      "title": "The Plan - Loyola Marymount University",
      "url": "https://resources.lmu.edu/strategicplan2021-2026/theplan/",
      "summary": "Loyola Marymount University's strategic plan for 2021-2026, titled 'Creating the World We Want to Live In,' envisions the formation of ethical leaders capable of tackling global challenges. It establishes three main commitments: Anti-Racism, Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion; Innovation and Adaptability; and Extending Our Reach Beyond the Bluff. The plan includes five spotlight initiatives, each with distinct goals and objectives, aimed at driving the university toward its strategic vision.",
      "stored": false,
